precated. Shows a warning when the block is used.&#x22;,\n    type: &#x22;boolean&#x22;,\n    default: &#x22;false&#x22;,\n  },\n  deprecationMessage: {\n    description: &#x22;Custom message shown when the block is deprecated.&#x22;,\n    type: &#x22;string&#x22;,\n    default: '&#x22;&#x22;',\n  },\n  computed: {\n    description: &#x22;The entire block is computed by the provider (advanced use).&#x22;,\n    type: &#x22;boolean&#x22;,\n    default: &#x22;false&#x22;,\n  },\n}\"\n/>"},"323":{"id":"/docs/concepts/schema-39","page_id":"/docs/concepts/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/schema#schema","content":"Top-level schema for a resource, data source, or provider."},"324":{"id":"/docs/concepts/schema-40","page_id":"/docs/concepts/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/schema#schema","content":"`version` starts at `0`. Increment it whenever the shape of stored state changes (renamed or removed attributes) and implement `Resource.upgrade()` to migrate old state. See Schema migration for patterns."},"325":{"id":"/docs/concepts/schema-41","page_id":"/docs/concepts/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts/schema#schema","content":"Use `blockOpts` to set a description or deprecation message on the resource's top-level block (shown in `terraform providers schema` and the Terraform Registry) –"},"326":{"id":"/docs/development/debugging","page_id":"/docs/development/debugging","type":"page","content":"Debugging & troubleshooting","breadcrumbs":["terrably","Development"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/debugging"},"327":{"id":"/docs/development/debugging-0","page_id":"/docs/development/debugging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/debugging","content":"Attach a Node.js debugger, read structured provider logs, and fix common issues."},"328":{"id":"/docs/development/debugging-1","page_id":"/docs/development/debugging","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/debugging#attaching-a-nodejs-debugger","con