pment/debugging#proto-files-not-found-at-runtime","content":"With `terrably build` (the standard path) this is handled automatically — the proto files are embedded as SEA assets."},"352":{"id":"/docs/development/debugging-25","page_id":"/docs/development/debugging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/debugging#transport-error-while-dialing","content":"The Unix socket path changed between runs. This happens when you restart the provider in dev mode without updating `TF_REATTACH_PROVIDERS`. Copy the new export command from the provider's stdout each time."},"353":{"id":"/docs/development/debugging-26","page_id":"/docs/development/debugging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/debugging#terraform-state-becomes-inconsistent-after-a-schema-change","content":"If you rename or remove attributes without implementing `upgrade()`, Terraform may fail to read old state. Options:"},"354":{"id":"/docs/development/debugging-27","page_id":"/docs/development/debugging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/debugging#terraform-state-becomes-inconsistent-after-a-schema-change","content":"Increment `version` in your `Schema` constructor and implement `Resource.upgrade()` — see Schema migration for patterns."},"355":{"id":"/docs/development/debugging-28","page_id":"/docs/development/debugging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/debugging#terraform-state-becomes-inconsistent-after-a-schema-change","content":"Run `terraform state rm <resource>` to drop the old state and re-create the resource."},"356":{"id":"/docs/development/local-testing","page_id":"/docs/development/local-testing","type":"page","content":"Local testing","breadcrumbs":["terrably","Development"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/local-testing"},"357":{"id":"/docs/development/local-testing-0","page_id":"/docs/development/local-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/local-testing","content":"Two workflows for iterating on your provider locally — dev_ove