":"/docs/distribution#local-packaging-example","content":"Local packaging example"},"558":{"id":"/docs/distribution-16","page_id":"/docs/distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/distribution#why-distribute-as-a-binary","content":"Operators who use your provider should not need Node.js or Bun installed. A single-file executable application bundles the JS runtime into a single native binary — exactly like a Go provider — so Terraform can launch it with a normal `required_providers` block."},"559":{"id":"/docs/distribution-17","page_id":"/docs/distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/distribution#build-a-binary","content":"`terrably build` runs these steps automatically –"},"560":{"id":"/docs/distribution-18","page_id":"/docs/distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/distribution#compile-typescript","content":"Runs `tsc` using your project's `tsconfig.json`."},"561":{"id":"/docs/distribution-19","page_id":"/docs/distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/distribution#bundle-with-esbuild","content":"Produces a single CJS file with all dependencies inlined."},"562":{"id":"/docs/distribution-20","page_id":"/docs/distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/distribution#generate-a-sea-entry-point","content":"Writes a preamble that extracts embedded `.proto` assets to a temp directory at startup and sets `TF_PROTO_DIR`, then appends the esbuild bundle."},"563":{"id":"/docs/distribution-21","page_id":"/docs/distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/distribution#produce-the-binary","content":"Runs `node --build-sea` (added in Node.js 25.5.0) to inject the entry-point into a copy of the node binary. If run with Bun, runs `bun --compile` (added in Bun 0.6.0) to build a single executable binary."},"564":{"id":"/docs/distribution-22","page_id":"/docs/distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/distribution#sign-macos-only","content":"Runs `codesign --sign -` (ad-hoc signature required for execution on macOS)."},"565":{"id