environment-variables","content":"Environment variables"},"679":{"id":"/docs/reference/serve-6","page_id":"/docs/reference/serve","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/serve#serveoptions","content":"<TypeTable\n  type=\"{\n  socketPath: {\n    description: &#x22;Unix socket path to listen on. Defaults to an auto-generated path under `os.tmpdir()`.&#x22;,\n    type: &#x22;string&#x22;,\n  },\n  dev: {\n    description: &#x22;Dev mode: use an insecure socket and print the `TF_REATTACH_PROVIDERS` export instead of the handshake line. Equivalent to `TF_PLUGIN_DEBUG=1`.&#x22;,\n    type: &#x22;boolean&#x22;,\n    default: &#x22;false&#x22;,\n  },\n  protoDir: {\n    description: &#x22;Path to directory containing the `.proto` files. Defaults to the `proto/` directory bundled with terrably. Override when using a custom build pipeline.&#x22;,\n    type: &#x22;string&#x22;,\n  },\n}\"\n/>"},"680":{"id":"/docs/reference/serve-7","page_id":"/docs/reference/serve","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/serve#normal-mode","content":"Terraform sets `TF_PLUGIN_MAGIC_COOKIE` before spawning your binary. `serve()` validates the cookie, generates a self-signed TLS certificate (cached at `~/.cache/tf-js-provider/ssl_cert.json` for 7 days), starts the server, and prints the handshake on stdout."},"681":{"id":"/docs/reference/serve-8","page_id":"/docs/reference/serve","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/serve#dev-mode","content":"Set `dev: true` or `TF_PLUGIN_DEBUG=1`. The server uses an insecure socket and prints a `TF_REATTACH_PROVIDERS` line instead of the handshake. Copy the export into your shell and then run Terraform normally."},"682":{"id":"/docs/reference/serve-9","page_id":"/docs/reference/serve","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/serve#dev-mode","content":"See Local testing for the full workflow."},"683":{"id":"/docs/reference/serve-10","page_id":"/docs/reference/serve","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/serve#environment-v